1 OCCU Visconde de Torre de Moncorvo - title created by H.M. Queen Maria II of Portugal, first as Baron [5/23/1835], then as Viscount [7/13/1847]: Member House of Lords: Ambassador to Court of St. James: Knight Royal Household: Knight of
2 CONC  the Order of Malta.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} My great great great grandfather was Cristovao Pedro de Moraes Sarmento who was born in Bahia, Brazil on May 13, 1788.  He was married on January 12, 1828 to Amalia Jordan who was born on August 15, 1806. They had 
2 CONC at least six children counting my great great gradfather, Tomas Inacio de Moraes Sarmdento.  The widower Cristovao was married for the second time on May 23, 1843 to Carolina Guilhermina Jordan who was born on June 11, 1809.  They
2 CONC  had at least one child.
2 CONT
2 CONT The title Visconde de Torre de Moncorvo or Viscount de Torre de Moncorvo was created by H.M. Queen Maria II, of Portugal, first as Baron by decree dated May 23, 1835 in favor of the aforesaid Cristovao Pedro de Moraes Sarmento; th
2 CONC en as Viscount by decree dated July 13, 1847 in favor of the siad Cristovao de Moraes Sarmento.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1st Viscount de Torre de Moncorvo, Cristovao Pedro de Moraes Sarmento was a diplomat Charge d' Affaires in Copenhagen and London.  He served for around forty years as legate or Ambassador from the Kingdom of Portugal to the Co
2 CONC urt of Saint James.  His granddaughter, Maria Luisa de Moraes Sarmento Costantino, would write that he was a favorite of Queen Victoria.  Cristovao was a Member House of Lords, Knight of the Royal Household, Knight Great Cross of 
2 CONC the Order of Sao Tiago de Espada of Portugal, Knight of the Order of Malta, Knight Commander of the Order of Danebrog, Denmark.  The Viscount de Torre de Moncorvo or simply Viscount Moncorvo, Cristovao Pedro de Moraes Sarmento die
2 CONC d in London on January 11, 1851.     
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.dodouropress.pt/index.asp?idedicao=66&idseccao=571&id=5415&action=noticia
2 CONT --------------------
