0 @N6000000002322303196@ NOTE When her father abdicated the throne of Portugal in her favor in 1826, the
1 CONT throne was seized by his brother Michael (Miguel). Eventually, she became
1 CONT Queen in 1834, at the age of 14. She was married and widowed at once to (?).
1 CONT To her second husband, Ferdinand of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha, she bore 11 children.
1 CONT Her reign was marked by struggles between moderates and conservatives on the
1 CONT one hand, and democratic and radical elements on the other. A modified
1 CONT charter took effect that remained the Portuguese constitution until 1910.
